# 218 · A teacher in Claude Code's own terminal has its tools from its first turn

**Status:** `IN_PROGRESS` · **Version:** [v0.1.4](../roadmap.md#v014)

## What

On the lab, 2026-11-06, a rig ran its agents in their own terminals. Its first teacher ran in Claude Code, its second in Pi and then in Codex. In three of the run's four teachers' rounds (20:32, 21:33 and 22:33 UTC), the teacher in Claude Code wrote in its field notes that it had none of the advisors' tools (`list_files`, `read_file`, `read_diff`, `kb_search`, the research tools), while the other teacher in the same round read the champion's code and cited its files and lines. In the fourth round (23:48 UTC) its notes cite files and lines too, and say nothing of missing tools. Its prompt had the same sections in all four rounds.

The supervisor serves the advisors' tools over MCP on localhost for each call and gives Claude Code the server with `--mcp-config` ([the terminal profile](../../../src/supervisor/advisors/terminal/profiles.ts)). The terminal host types the message once Claude Code's input box is up and its SessionStart hook has fired; nothing waits for the MCP server.

**Hypothesis (not checked):** in its own terminal, Claude Code connects the servers of `--mcp-config` in the background, and a turn that begins before the server is connected has none of its tools.

1. **The cause, from the record:** the call's transcript on the rig, which says what tools its first turn had, for a round without tools and the round with them.
2. **The message waits for the tools.** The supervisor serves the MCP server itself, so it knows when the program has listed its tools: the host types the message only after that, or after a limit, with the wait in the round's record. The same for the planner and every advisor in a terminal that gets MCP servers.
3. **A test** with the Claude Code stand-in that lists its tools late, and the real Claude Code acceptance with the advisors' tools.
4. **An advisor's Live lines over MCP.** `trial_session` reads a worker trial's lines alone, so an operating agent can't read the line item 2 writes, or any advisor's: a tool, or `trial_session` with an advisor's source (`advisor:<name>`), gives them, with the round's call.

## Why

A teacher without the code tools reviews the run from its brief alone: its ideas cannot be checked against the champion, and it says so instead of advising.

## Done when

- [ ] Items 1 to 4, with tests.
- [ ] Pages: the advisors' terminal (Agents, lanes and the planner), and the changelog.

## Decisions

- None yet.

## Progress

- 2026-11-07 00:21 UTC: Goal written from a lab run's field notes, its prompts' records and the rig's settings.
- 2026-11-07 02:05 UTC: in the same run's fifth round (01:53 UTC) the teacher in Claude Code gave no portfolio at all: the merged by model wrote that only one teacher gave one. Why it gave none is to be read from the round's record with the cause of item 1.
- 2026-11-07 02:19 UTC: item 2 built, before item 1's cause is read: the supervisor's tool server notes when the program first asks for its tools (`tools/list`, `listed`, `supervisor/advisors/tools/mcp.ts`), and an advisor's call in its own terminal waits for it, at most 30 s, before its first message (`beforeFirst`, `agents/cli/call.ts`, `supervisor/advisors/terminal/call.ts`). Live says how long the listing took, or that it never came, which is item 1's evidence on the lab: a teacher whose tools were listed before its message, and that still had none, disproves the hypothesis. Tests: `tests/supervisor/advisors/pass/past.test.ts` (no list, then listed once the program asks), the profiles' fake. Page: Watch and steer an agent in its terminal. The test files have not run yet.
- 2026-11-07 05:03 UTC: on the lab, on 52801c6e, the teachers' round of 04:31 UTC had a portfolio from the teacher in Codex alone; the teacher in Claude Code's own terminal gave none, as in the rounds above, where in the 03:30 round (on 7462712f, with item 2) it did. Item 2's line, which says whether its program listed its tools in time, is on the run's Live, and MCP can't read an advisor's Live lines: item 4 added. The lab's infrastructure session reads the supervisor's log for it.
- 2026-11-07 05:12 UTC: item 2 was wrong, from the round's Live lines (the lab's infrastructure session read them): both teachers' lines said `had not listed its tools 30 s after it started`, at 04:31:31 UTC, while Codex and Claude Code started in their terminals at 04:31:44 and 04:31:46 UTC. The wait was awaited after the program's setup and before its host started, so it always ran out. Both teachers then used their tools (teacher-1 56 calls, teacher-2 37), and teacher-1's review was lost to a refused answer, not to missing tools (goal 226). Fixed: `RoleTerminal` awaits `beforeFirst` once, when the program is up and ready and before its first message (`agents/cli/terminal.ts`; `agents/cli/call.ts` passes it on), and the line says `30 s after it was ready`. Test: `tests/agents/cli/call.test.ts` (the wait begins with the program up and its start signal given, once, and the message goes in after it). Page: Run an agent in its own terminal. The test file has not run yet. Item 1 is still open: this round's teacher had its tools from its first turn without the wait doing anything.
- 2026-11-07 06:37 UTC: item 2 seen on the lab, on 3f6425c1: in the teachers' round of 06:32 UTC, Live said `teacher-2's program listed its tools 20.2 s after its tool server started` and `teacher-1's program listed its tools 31.1 s after its tool server started`, and both teachers' messages went in after that. The test of the wait's order passed on the lab's test machine (3f6425c1, 24 of 24 with the other touched files). Item 1's cause in the rounds of 2026-11-06 is still not read from their transcripts, and item 4 is not built.

